{"name":"Watchet","hex":"#8fbabc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Watchet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A harbour town and civil parish with a town council                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  in Somerset, England, previously in Somerset West and Taunton district ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Watchet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Watchet","blocks":[{"text":"Watchet is a harbour town and civil parish in Somerset, England. It is situated 15 miles (24 km) west of Bridgwater, 15 miles (24 km) north-west of Taunton, and 9 miles (14 km) east of Minehead. The town lies at the mouth of the Washford River on Bridgwater Bay, part of the Bristol Channel, and on the edge of Exmoor National Park. At the 2021 census, the parish had a population of 3,948."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Watchet.jpg/330px-Watchet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watchet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Swain_Street%2C_Watchet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1889557.jpg/500px-Swain_Street%2C_Watchet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1889557.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Swain_Street%2C_Watchet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1889557.jpg/500px-Swain_Street%2C_Watchet_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1889557.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View along Swain Street, Watchet","link":"https://en.wikip